  "hard_rules": [
    "Every valid inquiry ends in a canonical determination or a precisely identified TRUE_CONFLICT.",
    "No prior record is a canonical-completion trigger, not a reason to stop.",
    "STAGING and UNKNOWN are not valid final ACE determination statuses.",
    "ACE searches for and prefers registered specialist capabilities before connective synthesis.",
    "Every answer field records its producer, source references, and run receipts.",
    "Operational failure is EXECUTION_BLOCKED and must not be misreported as canon uncertainty.",
    "The owner establishes invariants, reserved decisions, and delegation policy rather than selecting routine values.",
    "A new result is not labeled GENERATED_CANON or CANON_REVISION until its authoritative commit is recorded.",
    "Commit approval persists a determination; it does not reopen routine value selection.",
    "Root, nested-repository, and L1/L2/L3 boundaries remain explicit.",
    "A tool-specific projection never replaces the referent-preserving canon graph.",
    "Mutable capability calls record baseline, post-state, and concurrency policy.",
    "Semantic reproducibility is evaluated separately from byte-level artifact identity.",
    "A tool-native STAGING status is adapter input or provenance, never a final ACE determination."
  ],
